From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Complete video MFT drain with NEED_MORE_INPUT

Media Foundation drains a transform before applying a non-dynamic input
format change. Once all output has been consumed, ProcessOutput is expected
to return MF_E_TRANSFORM_NEED_MORE_INPUT. The media session uses that result
to apply the pending format and resume input delivery.

The winedmo video decoder instead translated the Unix decoder's terminal
STATUS_END_OF_FILE into MF_E_END_OF_STREAM. This left the format change queued
and prevented subsequent compressed samples from reaching ProcessInput. Lords
of the Fallen exercises this during H.264 playback initialization.

Treat terminal drain status as an exhausted input queue, matching the MFT
contract and the previous WineGStreamer decoder behavior.
---
 dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
index 11111111111..22222222222 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -1600,7 +1600,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI transform_ProcessOutput(IMFTransform *iface, DWORD flags, D
     else if (ntstatus == STATUS_END_OF_FILE)
     {
         samples->dwStatus = MFT_OUTPUT_DATA_BUFFER_NO_SAMPLE;
-        hr = MF_E_END_OF_STREAM;
+        hr = MF_E_TRANSFORM_NEED_MORE_INPUT;
     }
     else
     {
